    <l n="1" para="true">2. Quid si plures codices differant? | 3.</l>
    <l n="2">Quid si copia superfit testamenti.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">4. Duorum voluntas uno codice compre-</l>
    <l n="4">hendi potest.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">5. Quid moribus, &amp; an talis voluntas al-</l>
    <l n="6">tero invito ab altero possit revocari?</l>
    <l n="7" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 14.</l>
    <l n="8" para="true">1. <i>Quid sit testamentum nuncupativum?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">2. <i>An moribus omnis voluntas sit nuncu-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>pativa?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" type="heading" level="1" para="true">LIBR. 2. TIT. II.</l>
    <l n="12" type="heading" level="1">De Militari testamento.</l>
    <l n="13" type="heading" level="2" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">1. Testamentum militare, non sem-</l>
    <l n="15">per est militis, &amp; vice versa.</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">2. Miles describitur.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">3. Definitur testamentum militare.</l>
    <l n="18" para="true">4. Imperitia privilegii fuit occasio.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">5. Miles quomodocumque velit, testari po-</l>
    <l n="20">terit.</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">6. Qua requisita testamenti nuncupativi?</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">7. Qua testamenti scripti?</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">8. In expeditione demum testantur.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">9. Non si degant in locis limitaneis.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">10. Secus quam obtinet, si licentia impe-</l>
    <l n="26">ratoris propter infirmitatem, castra</l>
    <l n="27">excesserint.</l>
    <l n="28" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="29" para="true">1. Privilegium militare cernitur in</l>
    <l n="30">multis.</l>
    <l n="31" para="true">2. Vel nutu testamentum condit.</l>
    <l n="32" para="true">3. Pagani poterunt de moribus pro parte</l>
    <l n="33">testati pro parte intestati discedere.</l>
    <l n="34" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="35" para="true">1. Mutus &amp; surdus miles testari poterit.</l>
    <l n="36" para="true">2. Qui non potest scribere de facto non po-</l>
    <l n="37">test suam declarare voluntatem.</l>
    <l n="38" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="39" para="true">Veterani gaudent privilegio Veteran̄ gaudiū privilegio.</l>
    <l n="40" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="41" para="true">
      <i>Ante militiam factum testamentum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="42">
      <i>valet quasi ex nova militis voluntate.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="43" para="true">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="44" para="true">1. <i>Capitis damnatus testari potest.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="45" para="true">2. <i>Variis in casibus testari non potest.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="46" para="true">3. <i>Minima capitis deminutione non</i>
    </l>
    <l n="47">
      <i>fit irritum testamentum militis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="48" para="true">§. 6.</l>
    <l n="49" para="true">1. <i>Quis miles togatus?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="50" para="true">2. <i>Et quomodo testetur?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="51" para="true">3. <i>Nostri temporis milites privilegia me-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="52">
      <i>rentur militaria.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="53" type="heading" level="1" caput="12" para="true">LIBR. 2. TIT. 12.</l>
    <l n="54" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Quibus non est permissum facere testamentum.</l>
    <l n="55" para="true">1. <i>Nemo testamentum facit nisi cui</i>
    </l>
    <l n="56">
      <i>hoc permissum.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="57" para="true">2. <i>Cur filius familias nequeat testari?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="58" para="true">3. <i>Servus testari non potest.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="59" para="true">4. <i>Neque qui de statu suo dubitat.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="60" para="true">5. <i>Neque peregrinus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="61" para="true">6. <i>Neque haereticus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="62" para="true">7. <i>Neque damnatus capitis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="63" para="true">8. <i>Mores explicantur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="64" para="true">9. <i>Enarratur jus Canonicum.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="65" para="true">10. <i>Privilegium castrensis peculii multiplex.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="66" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="67" para="true">1. <i>Impuberes testari nequeunt.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="68" para="true">2. <i>Idem de furiosis statuendum.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="69" para="true">3. <i>Quid de substitutis dicendum?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="70" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="71" para="true">1. <i>Prodigus testari non potest.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="72" para="true">2. <i>Moribus quandoque potest.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="73" para="true">§. 3.</l>
  </main_text>
